>
> I agree. The focus of this new wiki should be the promotion on works in 
> Lojban and the indication of where to find learning resources. We should 
> aim to make it as user-friendly and up to date as possible (the old wiki's 
> dead links can be a pain) so that nintadni will have an easy time learning 
> the language. We should try to promote the community as being warm and open.
> What I think would be neat is that we could try maintaining some kind of 
> roster of jbopre, with self-reported levels of proficiency, activity in the 
> community, and a list of works produced or other community contributions.
>

Probably this is realised through additional templates. It's absolutely not 
a problem provided that you give me some links to Mediawiki-based (i.e. ~ 
looking the same as Wikipedia) web-sittes that have such feature. Then I'll 
do the rest of work to import that feature too LMW. 

